{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>החול</b> — twice here, and the other is כובד האבן ונטל החול. Once a distinction is made between sacred and profane at the departure of Shabbat, there is כובד האבן ונטל החול, for a person is heavy at the departure of Shabbat on account of the soul that was lost." "<b>יין ושכר</b> — and adjacent to it is ולהבדיל, for the havdalah blessing is recited over wine."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {1 "The phrase כובד האבן ונטל החול (\"weight of the stone and he took the sand\") appears to be a fixed expression or idiom; its exact referent is uncertain and may relate to a known parable or medical/astronomical tradition. I have left it untranslated as a proper-noun-like phrase."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:10.184725043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}